    <statement><p>Find the zero(s) (if any) of the function <m>y = x^2 - 9 x + 20</m></p>
<p>Enter your answer as a comma separated list.  If no real zeros exist, enter <alert> NONE </alert>.</p>
<p>The zero(s) is/are <m>x =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4, 5</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>  SOLUTION </alert>



To find the zeros, we solve the equation <m>0 = x^2 - 9 x + 20</m> . We see that this is factorable, as <m>y = (x - 4)(x - 5)</m>.
Therefore, the zeros occur where <m>x= 4</m> and <m>x= 5</m>.



</solution>
